# Who Am I? — project rules

## Standing product decisions (do not re-ask; survive context compaction)

- **English only.** No Dutch, no `next-intl`, no `[locale]` routes, no language switch, no `nl.json`. Spec v1.0 EN+NL is superseded by `WHO_AM_I_CURSOR_BRIEF.md` v1.2+.
- **Brief wins** over `WHO_AM_I_SPEC.md` on any conflict. Briefs are local/gitignored; this rule file and `REPORT.md` are the committed memory.
- **Phase gate:** After each phase, stop until the owner replies `continue`. Do not skip ahead.
- **Default selector:** fixed 10-item form until real data justifies adaptive.
- **Colours / LLM reword / free text:** flags off (`ENABLE_COLOURS`, `ENABLE_LLM_REWORD`, `ENABLE_FREE_TEXT` = false).
- Phases 0–1 are done. Next is Phase 2 (core UI) when the owner says continue.

## Hard rules

- **Engine purity:** `src/engine/` is pure TypeScript — no React/DOM imports. Deterministic given a seed.
- **No invented psychometrics:** Item parameters in-repo are DEV PLACEHOLDERS until calibrated ones are supplied. Never invent loadings, thresholds, norms, or accuracy numbers.
- **UI numbers from config only:** Never claim accuracy, reliability, or correlation in the UI unless the value is read from the model-version config (`ACCURACY_CLAIMS`, etc.). Empty claims ⇒ omit numbers.
- **Prototype banner:** While `bankStatus` is `dev-uncalibrated`, show "Prototype - scores not calibrated".
- **No storage before consent:** Zero network calls to the storage backend until the user explicitly consents. Default path is client-only.
- **Drafts never ship:** LLM-drafted or unreviewed user-facing content must carry `reviewStatus: "draft"` and must not be included in production builds unless `ALLOW_DRAFT_CONTENT=true`.
- **Immutable item ids:** Changing item text requires a new id; retire the old id. Never mutate text under an existing id.
- **Out of scope:** accounts, facets, PDF export, extra languages, career/relationship advice.
